Item A -- accidental-overhead micro-opts on the per-decode-step host path.

Five edits across two installed files, each individually below the ~0.5 ms A/B noise
floor and therefore landed as a batch on mechanism, not on a measurement:

  model_runner.py
    1. `sampler.apply_staged_writes()` folded into the existing `if
       scheduler_output.scheduled_new_reqs:` guard. `Sampler.add_request` is the only
       writer into the sampler's staged state and runs only inside that loop, so on a
       decode step the call was 14 `copy_to_uva()` whole-array copies (plus a torch
       slice alloc each) over state nobody staged.
    2. `build_slot_mappings_by_layer` skipped iff `cg_mode == FULL and speculator is
       None`. `run_fullgraph` is a bare `graph.replay()` -- it never enters
       `set_forward_context`, so nothing reads the per-layer dict on that arm.
       PIECEWISE / mixed / eager steps still build it (attention.py:761 consumes it),
       hence a PER-STEP guard.
    3. `req_id_to_index` cached on the runner, keyed by `input_batch.req_ids` LIST
       OBJECT IDENTITY. The decode fast path reuses one InputBatch and never mutates
       req_ids; any new or reordered batch allocates a fresh list, so `is` is an exact
       "same batch" test.
    4. The full-`max_num_reqs` `np.minimum` into `req_states.num_computed_prefill_tokens`
       deleted; the single read site recomputes it batch-sized off the gather it already
       performs. CAVEAT, deliberate: the array is left STALE for out-of-batch slots.
       Verified safe -- the only other toucher is `RequestState.add_request`
       (states.py:109), which writes each slot on admission, and the only reader is the
       site that now recomputes.

  core.py
    5. The three per-step `@contextmanager` entries in `step_with_batch_queue` replaced
       by inline `try/except` + `dump_engine_exception(...)` + re-raise (identical
       diagnostics, and the two regions stay SEPARATE so the first still cannot catch
       `future.result()`), with `log_iteration_details` skipped outright when
       `enable_logging_iteration_details` is off -- checked once at __init__ into
       `_vtl_log_iters`.

Kill switch: `VTL_HOTPATH_MICROOPT=0` restores stock control flow byte for byte -- every
edit is an `if _VTL_MICROOPT:` with the untouched stock statement in the `else` arm.
Same in-file-env-read convention as mamba_align_precopy.patch. Compose ships "1".

Touches no file any other v0.25.0 patch touches (api_server, lfm2, mamba_hybrid,
rejection_sampler, short_conv, sampler), so hunks cannot collide.

